  "slug": "benefits-backlog",
  "section": "The Promise",
  "title": "Let the Software Say Yes",
  "subtitle": "A federal law is piling verification work on New York’s benefits offices, and the City should decide now that software may approve aid but never deny it.",
  "category": "Public Benefits",
  "skylineStat": "84.7% of SNAP applications processed on time by New York City in fiscal 2026, up from 39.7% in 2023",
