  "title": "A Child Welfare Algorithm With No Public Evidence That It Helps",
  "subtitle": "Since 2018 a model that families never hear about has picked which abuse cases get a second look, and the City’s new algorithm office should make it prove itself.",
  "category": "Child Welfare",
  "skylineStat": "About 3,000 of roughly 50,000 child welfare investigations a year are picked for extra review by a predictive model",
